Blocked: a multi-line body may not be passed inline with --notes/-n.

  command: gh release create v1 -R foo/bar --title v1 --notes $'line1\nline2'

Combining --notes "$(...)" with a heredoc stacks two layers of quoting, and a
mis-escape — a stray backslash before a backtick — ends up in the published
text.

Fix: write the body to a file (a scratchpad, say) and pass --notes-file
instead of --notes:
  gh release create -R owner/repo ... --notes-file /path/to/body.md
